= render 'admin/breadcrumb_header'

- open_now = @window.read_only.present?
- source   = @window.source.presence
.admin-registry.my-3
  %header.admin-registry__head
    %span.admin-registry__title
      %i.fa-solid.fa-screwdriver-wrench{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
      Maintenance window
      %span.admin-registry__count= open_now ? 'Read-only' : 'Accepting writes'
    .admin-registry__head-actions
      %span.admin-registry__subtitle
        %i.fa-solid.fa-lock{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
        Admin-only

  .p-3
    %p.text-body-secondary
      A window makes the whole repository read-only. Searching, browsing and
      downloading carry on; depositing, editing and every other write are
      refused until it is closed. Use one before a migration or a risky deploy.

    - if open_now
      .well.p-3.my-3.rounded-3
        %dl.mb-0
          %dt.text-uppercase.small.text-body-secondary Opened by
          %dd= source == 'deploy' ? 'The deploy orchestrator' : 'An operator'
          - if @window.since.present?
            %dt.text-uppercase.small.text-body-secondary Since
            %dd= @window.since
          - if @window.message.present?
            %dt.text-uppercase.small.text-body-secondary Message
            %dd= @window.message

      %p.text-body-secondary.small
        Closing here clears the window whichever door opened it, including one
        the deploy opened. Background jobs are not resumed by this page — if the
        deploy paused the queues, it resumes them when it finishes.

      = button_to close_maintenance_path, method: :delete, class: 'btn btn-primary' do
        %i.fa-solid.fa-lock-open.me-1{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
        Close the window
    - else
      = form_with url: open_maintenance_path, method: :post, class: 'well p-3 my-3 rounded-3' do |f|
        .mb-3
          = f.label :message, 'Message for the banner (optional)', class: 'form-label'
          = f.text_field :message, class: 'form-control',
                                   placeholder: 'Scheduled maintenance until 10:00'
          .form-text
            Shown on every page and on the page a refused write lands on. Say
            when you expect to be finished.
        .mb-3
          = f.label :retry_after, 'Ask callers to retry after (seconds, optional)', class: 'form-label'
          = f.number_field :retry_after, class: 'form-control', min: 1, style: 'max-width: 12rem;'
        %p.text-body-secondary.small
          Opening a window does not pause background jobs. A job already queued
          will keep trying to write and will be refused, so drain the queues
          first for anything other than a quick look.
        = f.submit 'Open the window', class: 'btn btn-primary'
